## 🚨 CRITICAL — Must Fix Before Production

### 1. `.env` File Contains REAL Secrets Committed to Version Control

> [!CAUTION]
> **File:** [.env](file:///d:/Projects/QuitApp/backend/.env)
> **Lines:** 11-19

The `.env` file contains **actual Supabase database credentials, JWT secrets, anon keys, and service role keys**. Even though `.gitignore` includes `.env`, if this was ever committed to git history (which it appears it was based on the file existing in the project), these secrets are permanently exposed.

**Impact:** Full database access, JWT forgery, admin-level Supabase API access.  
**Fix:** Rotate ALL Supabase credentials immediately. Verify `.env` was never committed via `git log --all -- .env`.

