### 3. `AnalyticsService.getGlobalStats()` — NPE Risk on Null Aggregates

> [!WARNING]
> **File:** [AnalyticsService.java](file:///d:/Projects/QuitApp/backend/src/main/java/com/unshackled/api/service/AnalyticsService.java#L175-L177)

```java
long totalUsers = jdbcTemplate.queryForObject("SELECT COUNT(*) FROM users", Long.class);
```

`queryForObject` can return `null` when the result type is a wrapper class. On an empty database, `COUNT(*)` always returns 0, so this specific case is safe — but the `Long.class` unboxing to `long` is still a code smell. The real risk is on line 200 where `BigDecimal totalMoneySaved` could be `null` from the CTE query if no rows match.

**Fix:** Add null guards with `COALESCE` in SQL or use safe defaults after the query.

