## 🔶 MEDIUM — Code Quality / Logic Issues

### 13. `StreakService.recalculateStreak()` — Logic Flaw for Non-Consecutive Days

> [!NOTE]
> **File:** [StreakService.java](file:///d:/Projects/QuitApp/backend/src/main/java/com/unshackled/api/service/StreakService.java#L49-L71)

The current streak calculation starts from `LocalDate.now()` or `yesterday`. But if a user hasn't checked in today AND didn't check in yesterday, the current streak correctly drops to 0. However, the `longest_streak` calculation (lines 75-93) iterates chronologically but doesn't handle the case where there are multiple clean days separated by **gaps** (missing days with no check-in). A missing day without a check-in should break the streak, but the longest-streak logic only checks `prevDate.plusDays(1)` which handles it — EXCEPT it ignores the fact that a missing day isn't a "slip", it's an unchecked day. The architecture says streaks break on missed days, which is correctly handled. This is mostly fine but would benefit from a unit test.

