### 15. `AnalyticsService.calculateSavings()` — Missing Habit Slugs

> [!NOTE]
> **File:** [AnalyticsService.java](file:///d:/Projects/QuitApp/backend/src/main/java/com/unshackled/api/service/AnalyticsService.java#L219-L249)

The switch statement handles: `smoking`, `drinking`, `vaping`, `money`. But the architecture defines habit slugs: `smoking`, `drinking`, `vaping`, `chewing_tobacco`, `pornography`, `social_media`, `sugar_junk_food`, `gambling`, `custom`.

- `chewing_tobacco` → No case, falls to default (custom). OK if chewing tobacco doesn't have a separate cost model, but the architecture's schema has no specific columns for it.
- `sugar_junk_food` and `gambling` → Both use `spend_per_week`, should match the `"money"` case but the slug isn't `money`, it's `sugar_junk_food` / `gambling`.
- The case `"money"` doesn't match any actual habit slug from the seed data.

**Fix:** Replace `case "money"` with `case "sugar_junk_food", "gambling"` to match the actual seed slugs.

