### 29. `LeaderboardService.getFriendLeaderboard()` — SQL Injection via String.format

> [!WARNING]
> **File:** [LeaderboardService.java](file:///d:/Projects/QuitApp/backend/src/main/java/com/unshackled/api/service/LeaderboardService.java#L79-L83)

```java
String placeholders = userIds.stream().map(id -> "?").reduce((a, b) -> a + "," + b).get();
List<LeaderboardEntry> entries = jdbcTemplate.query(
    String.format(sql, placeholders), userIds.toArray(), entryRowMapper);
```

While the placeholders are `?` and the values are passed as parameters (safe), using `String.format` with SQL is a code smell. It's technically safe here since placeholders are generated from a controlled source, but it could be fragile. Also, `userIds.toArray()` returns `Object[]` of `UUID` objects — verify the JDBC driver handles UUID binding correctly.

