### 30. `WebPushService` — VAPID Key Validation Missing

> [!NOTE]
> **File:** [WebPushService.java](file:///d:/Projects/QuitApp/backend/src/main/java/com/unshackled/api/service/WebPushService.java#L43)

The `.env` has `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=your-vapid-public-key` (placeholder). The init method checks for `null` but not for placeholder values. The `PushService.setPublicKey()` call with a non-Base64 string will throw `GeneralSecurityException`, which is caught — but silently. Push notifications will silently fail with no clear log that the keys are invalid (only "Failed to initialize WebPushService").

**Fix:** Add explicit validation for key format/length before initializing, and log a clear error message.

